      "text": "### About the Author: Brian Christian\nBrian Christian is an American author and researcher recognized for exploring the intersection of technology, science, and philosophy. His notable works include:\n- **The Most Human Human** (2011)\n- **Algorithms to Live By** (2016, co-authored with Tom Griffiths)\n- **The Alignment Problem** (2020)\n\nFor a more in-depth view of his biography and works, you can visit his [author profile](https://openbooks.net/authors/brian-christian) and [complete works](https://openbooks.net/authors/brian-christian/works).\n\n### Reviews and Reception of *The Alignment Problem*\n*The Alignment Problem* delves into the challenges of aligning artificial intelligence with human values and intentions. It has received considerable attention, praised by reviewers for its insightful exploration of AI alignment and machine learning ethics. Key points include:\n- The book features interviews with researchers from various fields related to AI.\n- It has become an important contribution to the discourse on how technology aligns with human intent.\n\nFor further details, you can read about the book on [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Alignment_Problem), the [critical overview](https://openbooks.net/reviews/the-alignment-problem) of its reception, the [official publisher's page](https://openbooks.net/books/the-alignment-problem), and check its ratings on [Goodreads](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/50205298-the-alignment-problem) where it holds an average rating of 4.04/5 from 18,000 ratings.\n\nThese resources should provide you with a solid foundation for your review of *The Alignment Problem*.",
